===Etymology===
From Korean [[한글]] (hangeul), “Korean script” < Archaic Korean [[한글]] (hangeul) “great script”.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# The phonetic [[alphabet]] used to [[write]] the [[Korean]] [[language]].

====Usage notes====
The spelling [[han-geul]] is from the Korean spelling in the 2000 South Korean Revised transcription. “Hangul” is from the older [[McCune-Reischauer]] transcription “Han’gŭl” but written without the diacritics, which is often done. It a common English spelling. Within the English Wiktionary and in South Korea where this term is used (it isn't used in North Korea), “han-geul” is preferred as it is in accordance with the new Romanization and it clarifies against a possible (and incorrect) syllabization "hang-eul" or "hang-ul".

====Dictionary notes====
*'''MSN Encarta Dictionary''' lists only the spellings “Hangul” and “hangul”.
*'''Merriam-Webster Online''' lists only the spelling “hangul” and notes that it is often capitalized.

